## Result-file conventions read from experiment-repo (first real files, 2026-11-26)
- Method ids are those listed in experiment-repo#2 (`figtab/style.py` METHODS has all of them); an unknown id stops the build.
- Headline views (ladder, regime map, Table 1) use one interval construction per method, `primary_construction` in `config.json` (wald); E5/Table 2 shows all constructions.
- The floor has no interval: its row has `reps` NaN and a predicted `ratio_vs_ppipp`; it is drawn as a bar without CI and shown as "(predicted)" in tables.
- Excess widths (C1 panel) are divided by `pred_width_floor`, so real and synthetic cells share one axis. The diagnostic figure plots `pred_gain` against `realised_gain`; cells without `pred_gain` are counted in `tables/fig5_stats.json`, not drawn.
- `headline_n`: 500 per set, forest 200 (reference n fixed before the runs).
- Headline views use only `group == reference_grid`; stress, K=10, disjoint-draw and failure cells are other groups (stress and failure cells are in the regime map and `fig_breakeven_all_b`).
- A ladder rung / table column that no dataset has at the reference n is not drawn and is named in the caption note (B5 `select_x` has no row at the reference n so far).
- Appendix tables are `longtable` (header repeated); place them in single-column mode. `tab_constructions` shows the methods in `construction_methods`; `tab_full_grid` is the primary construction only and is a ledger, not meant for the PDF.
- Regime map outcome classes follow the pre-fixed margin: gain (valid, ratio CI upper bound < 0.95), no gain (CI inside [0.98, 1.02]), worse (CI lower bound > 1.02), undecided (valid, neither), invalid (arm misses the win rule), all fail (PPI++ misses it too). A class with no cell is left out of the legend and named in the caption note.
- `tab_constructions` uses narrow method names (`SHORT` in `tables.py`), `\scriptsize` and `\tabcolsep` 2 pt so it fits 6.75 in; widths of 1e6 or more (degenerate bootstrap-t at n = 25) print as mantissa and exponent.
- Not tracked (git-ignored, ledgers only): `tables/tab_full_grid.tex`, `tables/tab_not_run.tex`.
- T2 reference cells are complete (4 of 4 sets with X, alphafold in experiment-repo 81f15cd): the B5 column of `tab_main` and the B5 rung of the ladder are drawn.

- Two PPI++ baselines (Outline rev. 8): the package (`ppi-python` 0.2.3, tuning clipped to [0, 1]) is the reference of every ratio and of the pre-fixed classes; `ppipp_unclip` (same tuning, unclipped, same draws) is a ladder rung and a ratio column (`ratio_vs_unclip`, `headline.csv`). The floor is drawn in both units (asymptotic `floor_ratio` as a bar, `floor_ratio_measured` as a diamond); neither is a bound.
- `tab_main` second block takes classes from `headline.csv` and stops if its A6 ratio disagrees with `cells.csv`.
- Strongest valid baseline (Outline rev. 9): `tab_main` second block has the headline arm's ratio to the package PPI++, to the unclipped PPI++ and to the strongest valid baseline (`ratio_vs_valid_baseline`, `classification_vs_valid_baseline`; `base` = P package / U unclipped, double dagger = neither passes the coverage rule); the calibrated-spline ratio moved to `tab_headline_full` to keep the block within 6.75 in (checked: no overfull box).
- Fig 6 (`fig_clip`): the line is the formula for the population-optimal tuning, the markers include the estimation of λ; where they part (small n, b near 1) the figure says so. Only the σ = 0.6, N = 10 000 cells are drawn, the other cells are counted in the note.
- PDFs are not byte-identical between runs (random font-subset tags of the TeX route); a figure is re-committed only when its `.md` (the numbers drawn) changed.
- Neither-valid cells (Outline rev. 12): `fig_headroom_ladder` puts a double dagger above the headline arm (A6, and B5 on the T2 cell) of a cell whose package and unclipped PPI++ both miss the coverage rule (`baseline_valid = 0` in `headline.csv`); `tab_main` marks the same cells with a double dagger (T1: after the base letter; T2: after the B5 class). At reference n: T1 alphafold, census_income, forest; T2 alphafold, census_income (5 of 13, the Outline's 4 of 12 predates the alphafold T2 row). The regime map is unchanged: it classes against the package PPI++ and says where the class moves against the unclipped one.

Table 1 width (measured with `\hbox`, `\footnotesize`): first block 424.9 pt, second block (`\scriptsize`, `\tabcolsep` 1.5 pt, 13 columns) 478.6 pt, against the 487.8 pt (6.75 in) of a `table*`; at 2 pt it was 491.6 pt and overfull.

Labels in exhibits (paper-repo review of PR #9): no internal arm identifiers (A6, B5, B3, B4) and no panel title inside a graphic. Table 1 heads "Selected", "Selected, f and X", "Ratio, with X"; the base-class letters P/U are kept (spelled out, the second block would exceed 6.75 in); Fig 1 ticks "Selected" and "Selected + X" (the longer "Selected interval with X" made the figure 3.9 pt taller, and the page budget is tight). Sizes of all exhibits are unchanged.
